## Reflection
Answers:
1. Because inheritence gives the child class a few similarities to the parent. Additionally, food nutrients is the father class of vitamins and carbohydrates because both are types of nutrients. To further add, these can all be found in food, making it all relatable to food nutrients.
2. It gave the classes the same properties but just not the same structure. Nutrients could start off as the blue print for other classes making it less repetetive. Lastly, it can now focus on the application and not the replication.
3. My HAS-A relationship is Aggregation because the two objects can still exist independently. For example, a Food has Nutrients, but the Nutrient object does not completely depend on the Food object to exist. This makes it completely different from Composition.
4. it only shows how they interact in part 3. But in part 4, it has a stronger bond. This is utilized by the HAS-A relationship.
5. I used the DRY principle by utilizing other functions instead of the same ones. For example, I used Association and Aggregation instad of one singular relationship. I also used the differences of the types of nutrients to give variety.
